  "question": {
    "text": "A diatomic molecule has a dipole moment of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.2</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math>. If the bond distance is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mover></math>, then fractional charge on each atom is _____  <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> esu. (Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>18</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mi>esu</mi><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math>)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "0",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,</p><p> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.2</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mo>×</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mtext>where</mtext><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi><mo> </mo><mo>=</mo><mo> </mo><mtext>dipole moment</mtext><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mo> </mo><mo>=</mo><mo> </mo><mtext>charge</mtext><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>=</mo><mo> </mo><mtext>distance</mtext></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mo>=</mo><mo> </mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo> </mo><mo> </mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.2</mo><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mi>esu</mi></math></p><p>Hence, the charge present on each atom is approximately zero.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
